matplotlib.backends.backend_tkagg import FigureCanvasTkAgg\n 26 | try:\n 27 |     from matplotlib.backends.backend_tkagg import NavigationToolbar2Tk\n 28 | except ImportError:\n 29 |     # NavigationToolbar2TkAgg was deprecated in matplotlib 2.2\n 30 |     from matplotlib.backends.backend_tkagg import (\n 31 |         NavigationToolbar2TkAgg as NavigationToolbar2Tk\n 32 |     )\n 33 | from matplotlib.figure import Figure\n 34 | from matplotlib.contour import ContourSet\n 35 | \n 36 | import sys\n 37 | import numpy as np\n 38 | import tkinter as Tk\n 39 | \n 40 | from sklearn import svm\n 41 | from sklearn.datasets import dump_svmlight_file\n 42 | \n 43 | y_min, y_max = -50, 50\n 44 | x_min, x_max = -50, 50\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/utils/__init__.py:check_matplotlib_support`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1085 | def check_matplotlib_support(caller_name):\n1086 |     \"\"\"Raise ImportError with detailed error message if mpl is not installed.\n1087 | \n1088 |     Plot utilities like :func:`plot_partial_dependence` should lazily import\n1089 |     matplotlib and call this helper before any computation.\n1090 | \n1091 |     Parameters\n1092 |     ----------\n1093 |     caller_name : str\n1094 |         The name of the caller that requires matplotlib.\n1095 |     \"\"\"\n1096 |     try:\n1097 |         import matplotlib  # noqa\n1098 |     except ImportError as e:\n1099 |         raise ImportError(\n1100 |             \"{} requires matplotlib. You can install matplotlib with \"\n1101 |             \"`pip install matplotlib`\".format(caller_name)\n1102 |         ) from e\n```\n\nFound function `doc/conftest.py:skip_if_matplotlib_not_installed`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n102 | def skip_if_matplotlib_not_installed(fname):\n103 |     try:\n104 |         import matplotlib  # noqa\n105 |     except ImportError:\n106 |         basename = os.path.basename(fname)\n107 |         raise SkipTest(f\"Skipping doc