ping: Callable, default lambda x: x\n169 |         Callable to map the delegate's function to the cls' function.\n170 |     raise_on_missing: bool, default True\n171 |         Raise if an accessor does not exist on delegate.\n172 |         False skips the missing accessor.\n173 | \n174 |     Returns\n175 |     -------\n176 |     callable\n177 |         A class decorator.\n178 | \n179 |     Examples\n180 |     --------\n181 |     @delegate_names(Categorical, [\"categories\", \"ordered\"], \"property\")\n182 |     class CategoricalAccessor(PandasDelegate):\n183 |         [...]\n184 |     \"\"\"\n185 | \n186 |     def add_delegate_accessors(cls):\n187 |         cls._add_delegate_accessors(\n188 |             delegate,\n189 |             accessors,\n190 |             typ,\n191 |             overwrite=overwrite,\n192 |             accessor_mapping=accessor_mapping,\n193 |             raise_on_missing=raise_on_missing,\n194 |         )\n195 |         return cls\n196 | \n197 |     return add_delegate_accessors\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/core/accessor.py:_register_accessor`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n237 | def _register_accessor(\n238 |     name: str, cls: type[NDFrame | Index]\n239 | ) -> Callable[[TypeT], TypeT]:\n240 |     \"\"\"\n241 |     Register a custom accessor on {klass} objects.\n242 | \n243 |     Parameters\n244 |     ----------\n245 |     name : str\n246 |         Name under which the accessor should be registered. A warning is issued\n247 |         if this name conflicts with a preexisting attribute.\n248 | \n249 |     Returns\n250 |     -------\n251 |     callable\n252 |         A class decorator.\n253 | \n254 |     See Also\n255 |     --------\n256 |     register_dataframe_accessor : Register a custom accessor on DataFrame objects.\n257 |     register_series_accessor : Register a custom accessor on Series objects.\n258 |     register_index_accessor : Register a custom accessor on Index objects.\n259 | \n260 |     Notes\n261 |     -----\n262 |     This function allows you to register a custom-defined accessor class for {klass}.\n263 |     The requirements for the accessor class are as follows:\n264 | \n265 |     * Must contain an init method that:\n266 | \n267 |       * accepts a single {klass} object\n268 | \n269 |       * raises an AttributeError if the {klass} object does not have correctly\n270 |         matching inputs for the accessor\n271 | \n272 |     * Must contain a method for each access pattern.\n273 | \n274 |       * The methods should be able to take any argument signature.\n275 | \n276 |       * Accessible using the @property decorator if no additional arguments are\n277 |         needed.\n278 | \n279 |     Examples\n280 |     --------\n281 |     {examples}\n282 |     \"\"\"\n283 | \n284 |     def decorator(accessor: TypeT) -> TypeT:\n285 |         if hasattr(cls, name):\n286 |             warnings.warn(\n287 |                 f\"registration of accessor {accessor!r} under name \"\n288 |                 f\"{name!r} for type {cls!r} is overriding a preexisting \"\n289 |                 f\"attribute with the same name.\",\n290 |                 UserWarning,\n291 |                 stacklevel=find_stack_level(),\n292 |             )\n293 |         setattr(cls, name, Accessor(name, accessor))\n294 |         cls._accessors.add(name)\n295 |         return accessor\n296 | \n297 |     return decorator\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"AttributeError\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound class `pandas/errors/__init__.py:AttributeConflictWarning`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n648 | class AttributeConflictWarning(Warning):\n649 |     \"\"\"\n650 |     Warning raised when index attributes conflict when using HDFStore.\n651 | \n652 |     Occurs when attempting to append an index with a different\n653 |     name than the existing index on an HDFStore or attempting to append an index with a\n654 |     different frequency than the existing index on an