62 |         try:\n3763 |             assert_array_almost_equal(rank_proba, rank_score)\n3764 |         except AssertionError:\n3765 |             # Sometimes, the rounding applied on the probabilities will have\n3766 |             # ties that are not present in the scores because it is\n3767 |             # numerically more precise. In this case, we relax the test by\n3768 |             # grouping the decision function scores based on the probability\n3769 |             # rank and check that the score is monotonically increasing.\n3770 |             grouped_y_score = np.array(\n3771 |                 [b[rank_proba == group].mean() for group in np.unique(rank_proba)]\n3772 |             )\n3773 |             sorted_idx = np.argsort(grouped_y_score)\n3774 |             assert_array_equal(sorted_idx, np.arange(len(sorted_idx)))\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"assert_consistent_docs docstring consistency_check\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound `sklearn/utils/deprecation.py:deprecated`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n  4 | import functools\n  5 | import warnings\n  6 | \n  7 | __all__ = [\"deprecated\"]\n  8 | \n  9 | \n 10 | class deprecated:\n 11 |     \"\"\"Decorator to mark a function or class as deprecated.\n 12 | \n 13 |     Issue a warning when the function is called/the class is instantiated and\n 14 |     adds a warning to the docstring.\n 15 | \n 16 |     The optional extra argument will be appended to the deprecation message\n 17 |     and the docstring. Note: to use this with the default value for extra, put\n 18 |     in an empty of parentheses:\n 19 | \n 20 |     Examples\n 21 |     --------\n 22 |     >>> from sklearn.utils import deprecated\n 23 |     >>> deprecated()\n 24 |     <sklearn.utils.deprecation.deprecated object at ...>\n 25 |     >>> @deprecated()\n 26 |     ... def some_function(): pass\n 27 | \n 28 |     Parameters\n 29 |     ----------\n 30 |     extra : str, default=''\n 31 |           To be added to t