= ax.get_indexer_for(replacements)\n1049 | \n1050 |                 if errors == \"raise\" and len(indexer[indexer == -1]):\n1051 |                     missing_labels = [\n1052 |                         label\n1053 |                         for index, label in enumerate(replacements)\n1054 |                         if indexer[index] == -1\n1055 |                     ]\n1056 |                     raise KeyError(f\"{missing_labels} not found in axis\")\n1057 | \n1058 |             new_index = ax._transform_index(f, level=level)\n1059 |             result._set_axis_nocheck(new_index, axis=axis_no, inplace=True)\n1060 | \n1061 |         if inplace:\n1062 |             self._update_inplace(result)\n1063 |             return None\n1064 |         else:\n1065 |             return result.__finalize__(self, method=\"rename\")\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/core/internals/blocks.py:Block.astype`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n583 | def astype(\n584 |         self,\n585 |         dtype: DtypeObj,\n586 |         errors: IgnoreRaise = \"raise\",\n587 |         squeeze: bool = False,\n588 |     ) -> Block:\n589 |         \"\"\"\n590 |         Coerce to the new dtype.\n591 | \n592 |         Parameters\n593 |         ----------\n594 |         dtype : np.dtype or ExtensionDtype\n595 |         errors : str, {'raise', 'ignore'}, default 'raise'\n596 |             - ``raise`` : allow exceptions to be raised\n597 |             - ``ignore`` : suppress exceptions. On error return original object\n598 |         squeeze : bool, default False\n599 |             squeeze values to ndim=1 if only one column is given\n600 | \n601 |         Returns\n602 |         -------\n603 |         Block\n604 |         \"\"\"\n605 |         values = self.values\n606 |         if squeeze and values.ndim == 2 and is_1d_only_ea_dtype(dtype):\n607 |             if values.shape[0] != 1:\n608 |                 raise ValueError(\"Can not squeeze with more than one column.\")\n609 